# A Belgian HR software company sends employee data to service providers
# outside the European Economic Area. Under Chapter V of the GDPR a transfer
# needs an adequacy decision for the destination, appropriate safeguards such
# as standard contractual clauses, or, for an occasional transfer, a
# derogation such as the employee's explicit consent. The company's ODRL
# policy permits a transfer on each of these bases, adds a duty to assess a
# transfer that relies on the clauses, and prohibits sending health data.
# The snapshot allows the transfers to Japan, Switzerland, a certified US
# provider and, by explicit consent, a one-off relocation to Brazil. It
# prohibits the US analytics transfer that carries health data, reporting the
# conflict; it leaves the Indian helpdesk transfer undetermined until its
# assessment is recorded; and no rule applies to the bulk archive in Brazil.
# Shows an LE ODRL snapshot with rules: Logical English rules derive each
# transfer's observations from adequacy decisions, recipients and safeguards,
# and the snapshot evaluator decides, all with ODRL, DPV and GDPR prefixes.
# The adequacy decisions are input facts for this scenario, not a register of
# the decisions in force.
# Sources https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj (Articles 44-49)
#         https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/
#         https://w3id.org/dpv/2.3/dpv/ and https://w3id.org/dpv/legal/eu/gdpr

Use ODRL snapshot logic with namespace "https://example.org/data-transfers#".
Use prefix ex with namespace "https://example.org/data-transfers#".
Use prefix odrl with namespace "http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/".
Use prefix eval with namespace "https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyemind/odrl#".
Use prefix dpv with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv#".
Use prefix pd with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv/pd#".
Use prefix loc with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv/loc#".
Use prefix gdpr with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv/legal/eu/gdpr#".

# The adequacy decisions this scenario relies on. The US decision covers
# only recipients certified under its framework.

ex:japanDecision is a gdpr:AdequacyDecision and ex:japanDecision has ex:covers loc:JP.
ex:swissDecision is a gdpr:AdequacyDecision and ex:swissDecision has ex:covers loc:CH.
ex:privacyFramework is a gdpr:AdequacyDecision and ex:privacyFramework has ex:covers loc:US.
ex:privacyFramework is a ex:CertificationScheme.

# The providers and where they are established.

ex:payrollJapan has dpv:hasLocation loc:JP.
ex:pensionsSwiss has dpv:hasLocation loc:CH.
ex:supportDesk has dpv:hasLocation loc:US and ex:supportDesk has ex:certifiedUnder ex:privacyFramework.
ex:analyticsVendor has dpv:hasLocation loc:US.
ex:helpdeskIndia has dpv:hasLocation loc:IN.
ex:relocationAgent has dpv:hasLocation loc:BR.
ex:archiveBrazil has dpv:hasLocation loc:BR.

# The group policy: one permission per basis, with the assessment duty on
# the clauses, and a prohibition on health data that takes priority.

ex:groupPolicy is a odrl:Agreement and ex:groupPolicy has odrl:profile eval:SnapshotProfile.
ex:groupPolicy has odrl:assigner ex:hrCompany and ex:groupPolicy has odrl:conflict odrl:prohibit.
ex:groupPolicy has odrl:permission ex:onAdequacy and ex:groupPolicy has odrl:permission ex:onClauses.
ex:groupPolicy has odrl:permission ex:onConsent and ex:groupPolicy has odrl:prohibition ex:noHealthData.

ex:onAdequacy is a odrl:Permission and ex:onAdequacy has odrl:assignee ex:hrCompany.
ex:onAdequacy has odrl:action odrl:distribute and ex:onAdequacy has odrl:target ex:employeeData.
ex:onAdequacy has odrl:constraint ex:adequate.
ex:adequate is a odrl:Constraint and ex:adequate has odrl:leftOperand ex:adequacyCovered.
ex:adequate has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:adequate has odrl:rightOperand true.

ex:onClauses is a odrl:Permission and ex:onClauses has odrl:assignee ex:hrCompany.
ex:onClauses has odrl:action odrl:distribute and ex:onClauses has odrl:target ex:employeeData.
ex:onClauses has odrl:constraint ex:clauses and ex:onClauses has odrl:duty ex:assessment.
ex:clauses is a odrl:Constraint and ex:clauses has odrl:leftOperand ex:clausesSigned.
ex:clauses has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:clauses has odrl:rightOperand true.
ex:assessment is a odrl:Duty and ex:assessment has odrl:action ex:assessTransferImpact.

ex:onConsent is a odrl:Permission and ex:onConsent has odrl:assignee ex:hrCompany.
ex:onConsent has odrl:action odrl:distribute and ex:onConsent has odrl:target ex:employeeData.
ex:onConsent has odrl:constraint ex:derogation.
ex:derogation is a odrl:LogicalConstraint and ex:derogation has odrl:and [ex:occasional, ex:explicitConsent].
ex:occasional is a odrl:Constraint and ex:occasional has odrl:leftOperand ex:occasionalTransfer.
ex:occasional has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:occasional has odrl:rightOperand true.
ex:explicitConsent is a odrl:Constraint and ex:explicitConsent has odrl:leftOperand dpv:hasConsentStatus.
ex:explicitConsent has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:explicitConsent has odrl:rightOperand dpv:ConsentGiven.

ex:noHealthData is a odrl:Prohibition and ex:noHealthData has odrl:assignee ex:hrCompany.
ex:noHealthData has odrl:action odrl:distribute and ex:noHealthData has odrl:target ex:employeeData.
ex:noHealthData has odrl:constraint ex:health.
ex:health is a odrl:Constraint and ex:health has odrl:leftOperand ex:carriesHealthData.
ex:health has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:health has odrl:rightOperand true.

# The planned transfers: one request each, whose state records the
# recipient, the personal data and any safeguard.

ex:evaluation is a eval:Evaluation and ex:evaluation has eval:policy ex:groupPolicy.
ex:evaluation has eval:conflictStrategy odrl:prohibit.
For every T,
if ex:hrCompany has ex:plans T
then ex:evaluation has eval:request T and T is a eval:Request and T has odrl:assignee ex:hrCompany and
T has odrl:action odrl:distribute and T has odrl:target ex:employeeData and T has eval:subject ex:employees.
For every S, if S is a eval:State then S has eval:subject ex:employees.

ex:hrCompany has ex:plans ex:payroll and ex:payroll has eval:state ex:payrollState.
ex:payrollState is a eval:State and ex:payrollState has ex:recipient ex:payrollJapan.
ex:payrollState has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:Salary.
ex:hrCompany has ex:plans ex:pensions and ex:pensions has eval:state ex:pensionsState.
ex:pensionsState is a eval:State and ex:pensionsState has ex:recipient ex:pensionsSwiss.
ex:pensionsState has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:Salary.
ex:hrCompany has ex:plans ex:support and ex:support has eval:state ex:supportState.
ex:supportState is a eval:State and ex:supportState has ex:recipient ex:supportDesk.
ex:supportState has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:EmailAddress.
ex:hrCompany has ex:plans ex:analytics and ex:analytics has eval:state ex:analyticsState.
ex:analytics has eval:fulfilledDuty ex:assessment.
ex:analyticsState is a eval:State and ex:analyticsState has ex:recipient ex:analyticsVendor.
ex:analyticsState has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:MedicalHealth and ex:analyticsState has ex:safeguard gdpr:StandardContractualClauses.
ex:hrCompany has ex:plans ex:helpdesk and ex:helpdesk has eval:state ex:helpdeskState.
ex:helpdeskState is a eval:State and ex:helpdeskState has ex:recipient ex:helpdeskIndia.
ex:helpdeskState has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:Name and ex:helpdeskState has ex:safeguard gdpr:StandardContractualClauses.
ex:hrCompany has ex:plans ex:relocation and ex:relocation has eval:state ex:relocationState.
ex:relocationState is a eval:State and ex:relocationState has ex:recipient ex:relocationAgent.
ex:relocationState has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:Name and ex:relocationState has ex:frequency ex:once.
ex:relocationState has dpv:hasConsentStatus dpv:ConsentGiven.
ex:hrCompany has ex:plans ex:archive and ex:archive has eval:state ex:archiveState.
ex:archiveState is a eval:State and ex:archiveState has ex:recipient ex:archiveBrazil.
ex:archiveState has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:Salary.

# Article 45: an adequacy decision for the recipient's country, and for a
# certification scheme, the recipient's certification under it. Every
# observation is derived as true or false, so none stays unknown.

For every S and R and C and D,
if S is a eval:State and S has ex:recipient R and R has dpv:hasLocation C and
D is a gdpr:AdequacyDecision and D has ex:covers C and it is not known that D is a ex:CertificationScheme
or S is a eval:State and S has ex:recipient R and R has dpv:hasLocation C and
D is a gdpr:AdequacyDecision and D has ex:covers C and D is a ex:CertificationScheme and R has ex:certifiedUnder D
then S has ex:adequacyCovered true.
For every S, if S is a eval:State and it is not known that S has ex:adequacyCovered true then S has ex:adequacyCovered false.

# Article 46(2)(c): standard contractual clauses; Article 49(1)(a): an
# occasional transfer, whose explicit consent the state records.

For every S, if S has ex:safeguard gdpr:StandardContractualClauses then S has ex:clausesSigned true.
For every S, if S is a eval:State and it is not known that S has ex:clausesSigned true then S has ex:clausesSigned false.
For every S, if S has ex:frequency ex:once then S has ex:occasionalTransfer true.
For every S,
if S is a eval:State and it is not known that S has ex:frequency ex:once
then S has ex:occasionalTransfer false.

# The policy's prohibition reads whether the transfer carries health data.

For every S, if S has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:MedicalHealth then S has ex:carriesHealthData true.
For every S,
if S is a eval:State and it is not known that S has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:MedicalHealth
then S has ex:carriesHealthData false.
